{"uid":"e2684fe7124c63f2","name":"test_a_rejection_on_a_different_signature_is_not_bounded_by_an_unrelated_ruling","fullName":"tests.test_ruling_re_park_bound#test_a_rejection_on_a_different_signature_is_not_bounded_by_an_unrelated_ruling","historyId":"c3542df3f4562adcb9564602167a7c8d","time":{"start":1791931120940,"stop":1791931121125,"duration":185},"description":"A ruling addressing signature S1 must not silently cover a LATER\n    rejection whose own blocking-clause set (and therefore signature) has\n    changed -- the bound is per SIGNATURE MATCH, never \"any ruling exists\n    for this approach\".\n\n    Task 002 (PRD finding F02), extended in place: the SAME episode then\n    goes back to the ORIGINAL signature S -- the mechanical re-park lookup\n    must be keyed to the CURRENT rejection's own signature, never to\n    `status.json`'s `rejectionSignatures[str(approach)]`, which only ever\n    holds the approach's LAST recorded rejection signature and is\n    overwritten by every intervening rejection on a different one\n    (`_record_rejection_signature`) -- here, by the different-signature\n    rejection just above. The ruling filed against S must still spend its\n    one re-park once S recurs, whatever the intervening pause did to that\n    per-approach map; a further rejection on S then proceeds to the\n    ordinary archive/replan tail instead of re-parking a second time.\n    Every episode is a FRESH `LoopSupervisor` over the SAME on-disk run\n    dir, per this file's own multi-episode convention -- the bound is read\n    back from PERSISTED state, never from Python state a single process\n    happened to keep around.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>A ruling addressing signature S1 must not silently cover a LATER<br />\nrejection whose own blocking-clause set (and therefore signature) has<br />\nchanged -- the bound is per SIGNATURE MATCH, never &quot;any ruling exists<br />\nfor this approach&quot;.</p>\n<pre><code>Task 002 (PRD finding F02), extended in place: the SAME episode then\ngoes back to the ORIGINAL signature S -- the mechanical re-park lookup\nmust be keyed to the CURRENT rejection's own signature, never to\n`status.json`'s `rejectionSignatures[str(approach)]`, which only ever\nholds the approach's LAST recorded rejection signature and is\noverwritten by every intervening rejection on a different one\n(`_record_rejection_signature`) -- here, by the different-signature\nrejection just above. The ruling filed against S must still spend its\none re-park once S recurs, whatever the intervening pause did to that\nper-approach map; a further rejection on S then proceeds to the\nordinary archive/replan tail instead of re-parking a second time.\nEvery episode is a FRESH `LoopSupervisor` over the SAME on-disk run\ndir, per this file's own multi-episode convention -- the bound is read\nback from PERSISTED state, never from Python state a single process\nhappened to keep around.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791931120909,"stop":1791931120920,"duration":11},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791931120909,"stop":1791931120909,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791931120921,"stop":1791931120931,"duration":10},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791931120921,"stop":1